{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He was born around 1140 and became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\nRaymond III was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was a daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene. Raymond III was born around 1140 and became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father. He was only 12 years old when he became the count and his mother acted as regent until he came of age.\n\nRaymond III was known for his military prowess and his struggles against the Muslim forces in the region. He was captured by Nur ad-Din the ruler of Aleppo in 1164 during the Battle of Harim. He was held captive for several years and was released in 1173 after paying a large ransom.\n\n*The Regency of Raymond III*\nIn 1174 Raymond III became the regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem for the young King Baldwin IV. He was chosen for this position because of his experience and his military skills. However his regency was short-lived and he was removed from the position in 1176.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin*\nRaymond III played a key role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187. He was one of the leaders of the Crusader army and he advised King Guy of Lusignan to avoid engaging the Muslim forces in battle. However his advice was ignored and the Crusaders were defeated. Raymond III escaped the battle and fled to Tripoli.\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 shortly after the Battle of Hattin. He was succeeded by his godson Raymond of Antioch who became the Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0042634764686226845}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.25955715775489807}, {